## 9. Friend System and State Sharing

### 8 core + 4 close

Each user has 8 core friend slots and 4 close friend slots, totaling 12. Core slots are user-managed; close slots auto-fill from trailing 30-day `ClosenessScore`.

### What friends see about each other

- **Fuzzy state** (live, via cloud) — `thriving | okay | struggling`. Never the numeric score, component breakdown, goal type, or cycle phase.
- **Visible appearance** (cached, from last in-person handshake) — body, hair, equipped items, equipped bottle, accessibility items. **Background scenes are never synced.**
- **Send-heart button** — rate-limited to one per friend per day, server-enforced.

### Appearance syncs on meetup; fuzzy state is live

A friend's appearance is cached from your last proximity handshake. Fuzzy state updates live via the cloud so hearts-for-low-health still work.

**Appearance is about presence; state is about care — different cadences on purpose.**

### Activities with friends

One person creates an activity, others tap-to-join via the proximity handshake. Each logged activity increments closeness. Sole input to close-friend ranking.

### Close-friend demotion

Before auto-demotion, a soft notice appears: *"Sam hasn't been a close friend lately, mostly because you haven't done anything together in three weeks. Send them a heart or make plans?"* Demotion still happens on schedule; the notice is a chance to act. Non-repeating per friend per cycle.

### Hearts

Decaying bonus segments on the receiver's health bar (Minecraft golden-apple style). Decay over ~24h. Rate limit enforced server-side.

