## 10. Photowall

A place for photos of real moments. Sits behind the avatar as a fixed background element shaped like Polaroids on a string. Opens into a full gallery on tap. Photos occasionally surface on loading screens as ambient memory moments.

### Design goals

- Photos of presence, not curation
- Memory-surfacing that feels kind (filtered when the user has written negatively about someone in the photo)
- On-device only (encrypted, never in cloud)

### Placement on home screen

Fixed position in the background. 3–5 Polaroids in slow rotation, cross-fading every few minutes. Enable/disable but cannot move.

### Adding photos — proximity handshakes

One photo per participant during active handshake. Auto-tagged with handshake participants. Shared via Photo Booth card for 24 hours.

### Photo Booth (handshake after-party)

`PhotoBoothCard` appears on friend's profile. 24-hour lifetime. Keep/dismiss per photo. Passive presence, not a push notification.

### Adding photos — journal entries

One photo per entry. Camera opens by default; "choose from library…" behind an extra tap. Manual people tagging only (handshake metadata doesn't apply).

### People tagging — metadata only, never face recognition

Handshake metadata only. No Vision face matching, no face database.

### Memory-aware exclusion rules

`photoSurfacingExclusion` in Sensitive Memory. Negative journal text about a person triggers exclusion. Reversible via positive writing or natural language command. Falling off friend list is NOT an exclusion (mild surfacing preference for rekindling).

### Surfacing logic

1. **Hard filters:** excluded people, last 7 days, shown in last 30 days on same surface
2. **Preference weights:** positive journal days (strong), closeness-building activities (strong), ex-friends not excluded (mild), >1 year old (mild), never surfaced (mild)
3. **Random weighted pick**

### Loading-screen Polaroids

Normally ~1 in 10 loading screens. Bumped to ~1 in 4 when `moodTrend` is declining.

### Gallery view

Grid/scroll, filter by source/person, full-screen with metadata, copy to Photos Library via `PHPhotoLibrary`, delete from Fernlet.

### Storage and eviction

`PrivateMediaStore` with file-level encryption + CryptoKit key. 1000 photo hard cap. Warning banner at 900. FIFO eviction at 1000. Manual deletion anytime.

### Privacy and AI interaction

- Photos never sent to any AI model (Foundation Models is text-only anyway)
- Never transmitted off-device
- `Photo` type in `PrivateMediaStore`, unimportable by AI modules (compile-time enforced)

